        "title": "fix: prevent git push --mirror from hitting errors on force-push pin refs",
        "body": "Noted by @oliverpool in https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/15162#issuecomment-27459261.  The same approach as #14885 is used to allow the refs to be pushed by a `git push --mirror`, but the updates are discarded.  Both deletions and updates are ignored.\r\n\r\n### Compliance\r\n\r\n- [x] I confirm that I make this contribution in accordance with [Forgejo's AI Agreement](https://codeberg.org/forgejo/governance/src/commit/9084720dc6a7fbf1d3f358919d46bd6adfb55287/AIAgreement.md).\r\n\r\n### Tests for Go changes\r\n\r\n- I added test coverage for Go changes...\r\n  - [ ] in their respective `*_test.go` for unit tests.\r\n  - [x] in the `tests/integration` directory if it involves interactions with a live Forgejo server.\r\n- I ran...\r\n  - [x] `make pr-go` before pushing\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\n- [ ] I created a pull request [to the documentation](https://codeberg.org/forgejo/docs) to explain to Forgejo users how to use this change.\r\n- [x] I did not document these changes and I do not expect someone else to do it.\r\n\r\n### Release notes\r\n\r\n- [ ] This change will be noticed by a Forgejo user or admin (feature, bug fix, performance, etc.). I suggest to include a release note for this change.\r\n- [x] This change is not visible to a Forgejo user or admin (refactor, dependency upgrade, etc.). I think there is no need to add a release note for this change.\r\n    - Behaviour change in #15162, which is not released.\r\n",
